[Music]  today we celebrate and we remember  because we promised once that we would  never forget that brutal attack  on american lives american rights  and american soil by fundamentalist  terrorists on the morning of september  11  2001 i was teaching back-to-back  sections of american heritage  and in between the two sections a  student came up to me he was incredibly  flustered and he told me about the  events going on in new york city but  everything  was confused later that morning my wife  deidra  and i ran into president arn who  informed us  quite rightly that hillsdale would  continue to teach  all day because it's exactly what the  terrorists would not want us to do  2977 americans died on september 11th  my favorite story and one that never  ceases to move me is about one of the  passengers of flight 93  a man by the name of tom burnett who was  a 38 year old wall street banker  a father of three daughters and a devout  husband  he helped two other men drive a jet  airliner into rural pennsylvania soil  on that clear september morning we're  all going to die  but three of us are going to do  something about it i love you honey  those were his last words on his cell  phone to his wife  and i'm reminded of one of the greatest  of republican martyrs  marcus tulia cicero who was executed by  his own  executive in 43 bc and right before he  died  he wrote in a note to his son he said  before our time  the customs of our ancestors produced  excellent men  and these excellent men preserved our  ancient customs and the institutions of  their forefathers  but the republic when it came to us was  like a beautiful painting  whose colors were already fading with  age and our time has not only neglected  to freshen  the colors it has not even preserved  the original ones and it has not taken  the time  to keep together the frame its general  outlines  of the republic itself for what is now  left  of these ancient customs on which it was  said the republic of rome was founded  firm  they have been as we see so completely  buried in oblivion  that they are not only no longer  practiced they are almost forgotten  what would i ever say of these men  for the loss of our customs is due to  our lack of men  and for this great evil we must not only  give an account  but we must even defend ourselves in  every possible way  as if we were accused of murder  for it is through our faults not by any  accident  that we retain the name of republic but  have long since  lost its spirit cicero may have written  this in 43 bc  but could this not be america now and  yet  no matter what in this season of  confusion all of the sacrifices of 9 11  remain so let us remember those voices  who were silenced on 9 11. let us  remember the victims  let us remember the first responders let  us remember the heroes  may our colors never fade may our voices  never cease  and may our skies rage liberty and  sacrifice  you

